===Omni Strike===
:''This ability was added in [[Version 6.10 Update|Version 6.10]].''
Also known as '''Omnistrike''' or '''Omni-Strike''', this ability is similar to Long Distance, but the minimum effective range is always negative (or 0) instead; the maximum effective range still varies based on the unit, which can give them a form of "piercing range" without a blind spot. Cat Units rarely have such a luxury, so for them Omni Strike is primarily used for hitting [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] that burrow past them; the caveat is that units with Omni Strike can only damage enemies behind them if a target ahead is within their attack range for them to attack.

All Cats and almost all enemies with Omni Strike currently use Area Attacks, except rare cases like [[Mega Baa Baa]] and [[Balrog (Enemy)]].

Some units, such as [[Baby Garu (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Aegis Garu]] and [[Masked Okame]], have less than -320 inner range (320 is the size of a hitbox), causing them to have a blind spot within their hitbox where they cannot damage opposing units that somehow clip inside, notably Zombies, warped Cats, or very fast units clipping a knocked back opponent.

When close to the enemy base, units with this ability will stop at their maximum effective range instead of their standing range (if a unit has a Multi-Hit attack with varying ranges, this will always be based on the hit with the least max range of all the hits). A great example of this is [[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Great]], whose extremely long-ranged Omni Strikes can be used to cheese short-length stages while being safe in the back.

To better understand how this ability functions, see [[Hitbox]].

