==Trait-targeting Abilities==
Abilities in this section are listed next to '''Effect''' (効果, ''Kōka'') in the filter - with the exception of Toxic and Drain, which aren't listed there at all. They only affect indicated enemy types (targets), which vary depending on the unit. The Curse effect disables all abilities in this section.

Trait-targeting abilities used by cats with multiple targeted traits do not stack against multi-traited enemies such as [[Shy Boy]] and [[Bears Be Back]]. If the [[Fruit Treasures]] are not at an equal amount when used against such enemies (e.g., [[Blood Fruit]] at 100% and [[Sky Fruit]] at 200% against a [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy), the Fruit Treasure with a higher % will take priority.

Trait-targeting abilities that affect "all enemies" (e.g., [[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Asilan Pasalan]]'s Slow) do not work against [[:Category:Typeless Enemies|Typeless]], [[:Category:Witch Enemies|Witch]] and [[:Category:EVA Angel Enemies|EVA Angel]] enemies, which can't be "targeted" by these abilities in the same way as standard types like [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] and Red.

===Weaken===
Cats with this ability can decrease specific types of enemies' attack power, while enemies will weaken all cats. Effectiveness, duration and chance vary among units, with weakening units to 50% of their base attack power being the most common effect. The [[Fruit Treasures]] increase the duration of the effect against certain enemy traits by 20%. Although the icon for Weaken overrides the one for Strengthen, strengthened units under Weaken will still get the damage boost.

This ability is affected by '''"Weaken" Cat Combos'''.

