===Warp===
An ability exclusive to enemies despite appearing in the Cat Guide's filter. Depending on the success chance and attack type of the enemy, one or a group of Cats that get hit will disappear from the battlefield for a specific amount of time - provided they do not flinch or perish from the attack - and reappear a specific distance ahead or behind their original position. The duration and distance vary depending on the enemy; as of [[Version 15.2 Update|15.2]], [[Everlord Wanwan]] has both the highest warp distance (2000) and longest abduction time (66.67s). Cats being warped still count toward the Cat Deploy Limit. A unit with Sage Slayer that is warped by a [[Sage]] enemy will have their warp timer reduced by 70%, although warp distance isn't affected.

Since knockback takes priority over warp, units with very high knockback counts such as [[Gummy Cat (Special Cat)|Gummy Cat]] and [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]] will not be warped under most circumstances.

