===Curse===
:''This ability was added in [[Version 7.0 Update|Version 7.0]].''
Units with this ability have a chance to Curse enemies of specific traits, with the duration varying based on the unit. This effect completely nullifies the vast majority of the target's special abilities (if any) until the Curse ends, including '''Weaken''', '''Freeze''', '''Slow''', '''Attacks Only''', '''Strong Against''', '''Resistant''', '''Insanely Tough''', '''Massive Damage''', '''Insane Damage''', '''Knockback''', '''Dodge Attack''', '''Warp''', '''Curse''' (ironically), '''Toxic''' and '''Drain'''. [[Talent Orbs]] and abilities that aren't limited by trait target (Critical, Money Up, Zombie Killer etc.) are not subject to this. Since this ability functions by removing trait targets from Cat units, Cats with the "Target Only" ability will '''only''' attack enemy bases. The [[Fruit Treasures]] increase the duration of the effect against certain enemy traits by 20%.

Curse is applied after damage, meaning the initial hit from a Cursing enemy will not ignore defensive abilities like Resistant. For example, [[Miko Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Miko Mitama]] will take reduced damage from [[Relic Bun-Bun]] the first time it hits her, then take full damage from subsequent attacks due to losing her [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] Resistance.

Cursed units will display a small colored flame icon beside them to indicate that they have been afflicted with a Curse; green on Cats, yellow on enemies.

The Curseblast Cannon also has this effect.

