===Burrow===
:''This ability was added in [[Version 5.6 Update|Version 5.6]] and is not shown in the filter.''
An ability exclusive to [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie Enemies]]. Enemies with this ability will burrow underground when a Cat enters their range. Before going underground, enemies will perform a brief animation which leaves them vulnerable; if knocked back during said animation, their burrow will be canceled.

Underground enemies are invulnerable until they resurface, which happens after reaching the [[Cat Base]] or a certain distance depending on the enemy.

Most Zombies can only burrow '''once''', others never, but [[The Thrillerz]] can do this '''twice''', while [[Miss Haka]] and [[Big Sal]] can burrow '''as many times as they please'''. Since enemies set as bosses will immediately start an attack if a Cat Unit is within their range when they spawn, Zombie bosses that spawn under such conditions will first attack rather than burrowing, even Miss Haka and Big Sal.

As of [[Version 15.0 Update|15.0]], [[Znache]] and [[Zir Zeal]] have the longest burrow distance '''(1500)''', while [[Zroco]] has the shortest '''(375)'''.

''The Holy Blast [[Cat Cannon]] can damage underground enemies and force them to resurface immediately.''

For a list of enemies with the "Burrow" ability, see [[:Category:Enemies with Burrow ability|here]].

===Revive===
:''This ability was added in Version 5.6 and is not shown in the filter.''
This ability is exclusive to certain [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie Enemies]], and allows them to come back to life after a set amount of time. Upon death, enemies that can ''still'' revive will not drop any money, and will leave behind a purple puddle with a bone and skull to indicate where they will respawn. The puddle is harmless and cannot be hit or targeted by units without the Soulstrike ability, but still counts towards the enemy limit. Enemies with this ability have varying revival time, revive limit and remaining %HP after respawn. Any status effects inflicted are also passed on when the enemy does revive, although this is only apparent on those with very short revival delays or if a Soulstrike unit that has such abilities attacks the Zombie. Immunities carry over to Zombies' remains (e.g., the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast Cannon]] cannot push back the remains of knockback-immune Zombies).

As of [[Version 15.0 Update|15.0]], [[Death Angel Z-Onel]] has the shortest revival time '''(0.5s)''', while [[Formicidaean Ariant]] has the longest '''(24s)'''. Most enemies respawn with either '''50%''' or '''100%''' HP, except for [[Inumusha]], [[Big Peng Z]] and [[Daboo of the Dead]], which respawn with '''25%''', '''10%''' and '''10%''' HP respectively.

For a list of enemies with the "Revive" ability, see [[:Category:Enemies with Revive ability|here]].

