===Counter-Surge===
:''This ability was added in [[Version 12.4 Update|Version 12.4]].''
Counter-Surge is an ability that allows certain units to create their own Surge Attacks whenever a Surge hits them. If the same Surge hits multiple times, it triggers a counter only once, but if multiple surges from the same multi-hit attack hit, all will result in a counter. Visually, this is represented by a one-eyed soul with a colored aura (blue for cats, pink for enemies) appearing above the user, jittering for a moment, and firing off a Surge from its eye before returning to the user's body, taking a total of 1.7 seconds to execute. The Surge's level, type (Mini or normal) and spawn range are inherited from the attack that triggered it, while damage, debuffs and other effects come from enemy itself; when used by multi-hit characters like [[Kappy Kawano]], the damage is equal to the first hit of their attack. Unlike with Death Surge, Weaken and Curse remain fully effective

Note that units with Counter-Surge are still vulnerable to Surges, as they must be hit directly by a Surge generated from a normal attack for activation and not a duped Surge, so the ability can't loop. For example, if an enemy with a [[Shield]] and Counter-Surge gets hit by a Surge that does not punch through its Shield and damage it, the enemy won't dupe the Surge. Likewise, if an enemy with Counter-Surge dupes a Surge and hits a cat unit with the same ability, the latter won't return fire by spawning another Surge even if the duped Surge damages it. If a unit has both Surge Immune and Counter-Surge, such as when equipping a Single Counter-Surge [[Talent Orbs|Talent Orb]] on a unit with Surge Immune, Counter-Surge doesn't function at all.

