|}

For a list of Cats with the "Wave Shield" ability, see [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|here]].

===Conjure===
:''This ability was added in [[Version 13.1 Update|Version 13.1]].''
15 frames after deploying a unit with this ability, the text "Conjure!" will appear on its icon. The player can tap on the icon again to "Conjure" a spirit at no cost. This can be done only once per recharge cycle. Once that is done, both the Conjured spirit and parent unit can no longer be deployed unless the latter has been destroyed, although the parent unit's cooldown continues normally. As such, each specific Conjurer may only have up to one instance of themselves present at all times except via certain [[Otherworld Colosseum]] rulesets which spawn multiple copies of a unit at once. In this case, triggering Conjure will activate the ability on all copies of the unit currently on the field. If the parent unit is defeated before the spirit could be spawned, the "Conjure!" indicator disappears, and it will not be available until the next cycle. Though every spirit and its effects are unique, most have the same damage (45,900 with all treasures at level 30, scales with unit level, but not Plus Levels), range (800) and attack animation ([[Mamoluga (Uber Rare Cat)#Spirit|Mamoluga's Spirit]] has 1300 range and a different attack animation, [[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Squire Luno's Spirit]] has 600 range and 15,300 damage). 

The Conjured spirit is immune to Boss Shockwaves and has a 100% chance to dodge all attacks, including from animated bases and collab-exclusive traits. This ensures that it cannot die and its attack will not be disrupted, as it will despawn after that. This also allows for many cheese strategies to be possible. In addition, the Conjured unit occupies a spot in the Cat Limit and cannot be deployed when it is full.

When Conjured, the spirit appears 150 range behind the Conjurer, with some exceptions. The spirit cannot be Conjured behind the [[Cat Base]] (all units are deployed 100 distance behind the Cat Base), and attempting to do so causes the spirit to spawn exactly at the base. In addition, if the Conjurer is sufficiently close to the enemy base, the spirit will spawn farther behind the Conjurer so that the spirit's range reaches exactly to the enemy base, and will not hit anything behind it. If a Conjurer is in the process of being Warped by an enemy unit, the spirit will spawn based on the Conjurer's last stable position.

