*Many abilities were rebalanced or replaced in [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou|YuruGeGe]]:
**Slow only reduced units' speed by 66%, but also tripled their time between attacks.
**Curse was replaced by Seal (封印 ''Fūin''), which worked the same, but also disabled Yaba-Yaba (the ability to spawn minions upon defeating an enemy), even though Yaba-Yaba wasn't a trait-targeting ability.
**[[Barrier]]s were replaced by Forcefields (結界 ''Kekkai''), pentagrams which could only be destroyed by a Forcefield Breaker, not damage, and would be visible at all times, even when not being attacked.
**[[Wave Attack]]s in YuruGeGe originally didn't inherit special effects. However, this was later changed in an update.
**[[Surge Attack]]s were replaced by Secret Arts (秘術 ''Hijutsu''), which could have different effects/abilities and damage values from the attack that created them, as well as different designs and animations depending on the unit.
**Wave Shield only had a set chance to block waves, although the value was still 100% for most units.
**Burrow was replaced by Shadowization (影化 ''Kage-ka''), which worked the same, but caused its user to disappear into a smoky shadow that could still be seen moving across the ground, making it possible to determine their location before they resurface.
*Despite being exclusive to enemies, the Warp ability has been displayed in the filter since [[Version 8.0 Update|Version 8.0]].
**At an unknown date, [[Sunrise Doge]] became the first enemy to be given Immunity to Warp, which effectively changed nothing in regards to normal gameplay.
*[[Mesocosmocyclone]]'s negative warp enables it to teleport cats behind the enemy base under rare circumstances. [https://youtu.be/N_G5hryrIG8 When this happens], the cats will continue to walk forward until they go off-screen, disappearing from the [[battle]] but still counting towards the Cat Deploy Limit.
**Due to the nature of binary data, [[wikipedia:Integer Overflow|overflow]] will cause a unit past the enemy base to eventually teleport behind the [[Cat Base]] if left long enough, and eventually return to the fight. This phenomenon is seen in [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qdzAifKBYWU this video].
*The portals created when a unit is being warped resemble the portals from the game ''[[wikipedia:Portal (video game)|Portal]]'' in that the initial portal is orange while the secondary portal is blue.
*The soul that appears when the Counter-Surge ability activates resembles the top of the [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]] (which itself is modeled after the [[wikipedia:Monument to the Revolution of the people of Moslavina|Monument to the Revolution of the people of Moslavina]] in Croatia), as well as the boss [[wikia:kirby:0²|0²]] from ''[[wikia:kirby:Kirby 64: The Crystal Shards|Kirby 64: The Crystal Shards]]''.
*Kamikaze, Omni Strike and Multi-Hit were first introduced in [[Kumanchu Royale]].
*Surge Attacks, Mini-Surge and [[Explosion]] are the only abilities to have the same descriptions for enemies as they do for cats.
*Immune to Explosions' enemy description was added in [[Version 13.7 Update|Version 13.7]], but was unused until [[Version 14.3 Update|Version 14.3]], which added [[Baki Hanma (Enemy)|Baki Hanma]].
*In the files for the [[Enemy Guide]], there is an unused description for an ability named Immune to Damage. The ability has no icon in the files, isn't used by any enemy, and is not the same as Dodge Attack. The exact version it was added in is unknown, but it is placed before Toxic, which indicates it was before [[Version 9.1 Update|Version 9.1]]. In the [[Cat Guide]], the text is replaced by a placeholder.
:''【Immune to Damage】<br>This enemy does not take attack damage.''
*As of an unknown version, characters with 0 speed, such as [[Package Doge]], will no longer move forward when slowed.
*[[Retsu Kaioh (Uber Rare Cat)|Retsu Kaioh]], [[Komori (Uber Rare Cat)|Komori]], [[Juri (Uber Rare Cat)|Juri]] and [[Metal Maiden Koneko (Uber Rare Cat)|Metal Maiden Koneko]] are the only units to have Behemoth Slayer in Normal/Evolved Form rather than gaining it from a [[True Form]], [[Talents|Talent]] or Ultra Talent.
*Like Surge Attacks, Explosions have a parameter for a range in which they can spawn, but all current Explosion units have the width of this range set to 0.
*Prior to [[Version 13.4 Update|Version 13.4]], hitting a regenerated Aku Shield except via Shield Pierce would immediately cleanse all debuffs on the enemy regardless of remaining duration. This was presumably a bug.

